F-08 — CI is red on main by design, so a real regression is indistinguishable from the expected red
Started 2026-11-09 on main at 3041430. Owner instruction: "continue".

== State before any change ==
The "Authoritative explanation-content gate" (release_status.py --content-only) is a step at the END of test.yml's
backend job, after pytest. It exits 1 while content review is incomplete (measured today: exit 1, "content ready
False"), so the backend job, and with it the `test` workflow, fails on every push whether or not pytest passed - the
red the B8-F-20 live checks have had to read past as "every step green except the F-08 gate". A side effect: every
step after it is skipped, so the advisory glossary report (scripts/glossary_status.py, measured exit 0) has never run
in CI. The "Explanation review detail" step runs `adjudication_status.py --json || true` and
`review_status.py --json || true`; standing rule 3 forbids `|| true`, and here it also hides a crash, because a
Python traceback exits 1, the same code adjudication_status uses for "incomplete" (measured: adjudication exit 1,
review exit 0).
Already resolved by other work: the Deploy workflow no longer fails the same way (the gate amendment; every Deploy
since B8 succeeded).
Kept, with the reason: deploy-web.yml's `... 2>/dev/null || echo ""` in the /ready confirmation loop. Under
`set -euo pipefail` it turns a failed curl into "not confirmed yet"; the loop retries ten times, then errors. The
return code is handled and the step fails closed - it is not swallowed.
test.yml is read by scripts/compatible_bundle.py, but only its flutter-version value, which this change leaves alone,
so the bundle is unaffected.

== Criteria, written before the change ==
C1  The content gate and the detail reports leave test.yml and run in their own workflow, content-review.yml, with
    the setup the backend job gave them (dependencies, the spaCy model, JDK 17, the pinned binaries), so their result
    means what it meant before. `test` then reflects the tests alone.
C2  No `|| true` in any workflow. The detail reports' exit codes are captured and printed, and each run must produce
    a parseable JSON report, so a crash fails the step instead of passing as "incomplete".
C3  Guards: no workflow contains `|| true`; test.yml runs no `release_status.py --content-only`; content-review.yml
    does (it was moved, not deleted); its detail step validates the JSON.
C4  Both workflows parse as YAML; verify_compatible_bundle.py still passes; the backend suite passes.
C5  Sabotage, each restored byte-identical: `|| true` put back; the content gate put back into test.yml; the gate
    deleted from content-review.yml. Each turns a guard red.
C6  After a push, if the owner approves one: the test workflow concludes success, and content-review concludes
    failure on the content gate step alone. That is the property F-08 asks for, and only CI can show it.
